 surprisingly, led the qualifying, followed by Australia. The United States was the fourth qualifier, behind Great Britain, with somewhat of a B team swimming the heats."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was held on the first night of the Paris 2024 swimming programme. China put out their superstar sprinter, " [:a {:href "/athletes/154433"} "Pan Zhanle"] ", on the first leg, and he gave them a ¾-second lead over " [:a {:href "/athletes/154794"} "Jack Alexy"] " of the United States. On the second leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/154791"} "Chris Guiliano"] " put the Americans in front and they were never headed, winning the gold medal by over a second ahead of Australia. " [:a {:href "/athletes/136353"} "Caeleb Dressel"] ", the USA anchor, won gold in the event for the third consecutive Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Australia was not in silver medal position until the anchor, and stood fourth and third at the first two exchanges, but " [:a {:href "/athletes/132557"} "Kyle Chalmers"] " had the fastest split of the night (46.59) to bring them home in second. China went from first to last on the second leg by " [:a {:href "/athletes/141884"} "Ji Xinjie"] ", but would come back, finally finishing fourth behind the surprising bronze medalist, Italy."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:12.61 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "3:09.28 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/154794"} "Jack Alexy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/154791"} "Chris Guiliano"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147471"} "Hunter Armstron